{
	"info": {
		"_postman_id": "availability-booking-system-collection-v2",
		"name": "Provider Availability & Booking System (API Key Auth)",
		"description": "Complete test collection for the Provider Availability and Booking System.\n\n## Setup Instructions\n\n1. **Import the Environment**: Import the companion environment file\n2. **Start the Server**: Run `go run ./cmd/api/` from the project root\n3. **Register a Product**: Run the 'Register Product' request to get API credentials\n4. **Run Tests**: Execute requests in order from top to bottom\n\n## Authentication\n\nAll authenticated requests use these headers:\n- `X-API-Key`: Product's API key\n- `X-API-Secret`: Product's API secret\n- `X-External-User-ID`: User identifier from your system\n- `X-Role`: User role (admin, user, or provider)\n\n## Key Features Tested\n- Dynamic slot generation (slots are computed, never stored)\n- Double-booking prevention via PostgreSQL EXCLUSION CONSTRAINT\n- Buffer times before/after appointments\n- Timezone support\n- Concurrency safety with REPEATABLE READ transactions",
		"schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
	},
	"item": [
		{
			"name": "0. Setup & Health",
			"item": [
				{
					"name": "Health Check",
					"event": [
						{
							"listen": "test",
							"script": {
								"exec": [
									"pm.test(\"Status code is 200\", function () {",
									"    pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
									"});",
									"",
									"pm.test(\"Health status is ok\", function () {",
									"    var jsonData = pm.response.json();",
									"    pm.expect(jsonData.status).to.eql(\"ok\");",
									"});"
								],
								"type": "text/javascript"
							}
						}
					],
					"request": {
						"method": "GET",
						"header": [],
						"url": {
							"raw": "{{base_url}}/health",
							"host": ["{{base_url}}"],
							"path": ["health"]
						},
